{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463188",
      "title": "Methods used for Data Binding: How It Works",
      "lectureOrder": 30,
      "videoOrder": 26,
      "sourceHash": "750636be433100a492f8af755e9718b0712c7005193d0ca65f5d813668fa807a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.17,
          "end": 3.59,
          "en": "So now at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.59,
          "end": 5.87,
          "en": "we know a couple of things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.87,
          "end": 8.77,
          "en": "We learned about DOM interaction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.77,
          "end": 11.47,
          "en": "and that's a complex term with that I mean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.47,
          "end": 14.77,
          "en": "that we learned how to make a part of the DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.77,
          "end": 19.53,
          "en": "the template of our Vue app by mounting the Vue app to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.53,
          "end": 21.2,
          "en": "We learned about data binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.2,
          "end": 26.08,
          "en": "with the bind and string interpolation, and also v-HTML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.08,
          "end": 28.81,
          "en": "and we learned about event handling with v-on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.81,
          "end": 31.47,
          "en": "but also with v-model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.47,
          "end": 34.82,
          "en": "To be precise, v-model is two-way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.82,
          "end": 37.24,
          "en": "and therefore the combination of data binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.24,
          "end": 39.62,
          "en": "and event handling so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.62,
          "end": 42.26,
          "en": "Now, it's time to dive into a third,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.26,
          "end": 44.62,
          "en": "big block that makes up Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.62,
          "end": 46.69,
          "en": "This block has no official name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.69,
          "end": 50.75,
          "en": "but I like to call it advanced reactivity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.75,
          "end": 53.11,
          "en": "Vue is very reactive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.11,
          "end": 55.78,
          "en": "we already see that in a lot of places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.78,
          "end": 58.93,
          "en": "When I type here, the name here updates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.93,
          "end": 60.7,
          "en": "and Vue does that for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.7,
          "end": 64.223,
          "en": "The same if we change the counter, so that all works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.08,
          "end": 66.87,
          "en": "But we have even more features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.87,
          "end": 69.38,
          "en": "than what we know about thus far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.38,
          "end": 72.77,
          "en": "And I wanna start by coming back to methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.77,
          "end": 75.21000000000001,
          "en": "besides using them with events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.21000000000001,
          "end": 78.89,
          "en": "and then show you a better alternative to methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.89,
          "end": 80.513,
          "en": "for certain use cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.49,
          "end": 84.84,
          "en": "Now, in this app here, we add it to a binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.84,
          "end": 89.8,
          "en": "but to add it, we had to get rid of our last name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.8,
          "end": 91.41,
          "en": "Now, that's not too bad",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.41,
          "end": 94.72,
          "en": "because the way we made the entered name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.72,
          "end": 99.66,
          "en": "a full name by adding a last name wasn't ideal anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.66,
          "end": 103.72999999999999,
          "en": "using this setName method, passing in this argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.72999999999999,
          "end": 107.47,
          "en": "it worked but as you see, as soon as you want to do more,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.47,
          "end": 110.47,
          "en": "for example, adding a reset functionality,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.47,
          "end": 113.92,
          "en": "it's pretty hard to implement it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.92,
          "end": 116.2,
          "en": "that's why we had to get rid of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.2,
          "end": 120.68,
          "en": "But that's no problem, we can output a full name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.68,
          "end": 122.63,
          "en": "in a different way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.63,
          "end": 124.92,
          "en": "For example, we can add a new method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.92,
          "end": 127.08,
          "en": "anywhere where you want` by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.08,
          "end": 130.18,
          "en": "the order of methods here does not play a role.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.18,
          "end": 132.47,
          "en": "So I will add it at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.47,
          "end": 135.257,
          "en": "And we'll name it, outputFullname,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.1,
          "end": 140.86,
          "en": "because that's what this method should do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.86,
          "end": 145.09,
          "en": "It should return something, because I'm not going to use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.09,
          "end": 146.97,
          "en": "to bind it to an event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.97,
          "end": 151.23,
          "en": "but instead I'm going to use it to call it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.23,
          "end": 152.5,
          "en": "in the curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.5,
          "end": 155.793,
          "en": "I wanna call outputFullname, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.68,
          "end": 159.56,
          "en": "And therefore I wanna get back to full name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.56,
          "end": 164.53,
          "en": "which then will be inserted in this part of the HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.53,
          "end": 167.4,
          "en": "And therefore here I wanna return this name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.4,
          "end": 169.06,
          "en": "which is the entered name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.06,
          "end": 172.723,
          "en": "so this name property, which we're managing with v-model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.93,
          "end": 178.683,
          "en": "plus a blank space, plus Schwarzmuller,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.07,
          "end": 183.27,
          "en": "and of course this Schwarzmuller could also be fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.27,
          "end": 186.463,
          "en": "from another input, here it's simply hard-coded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.64,
          "end": 189.92,
          "en": "And if it's now saved and then reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.92,
          "end": 192.38,
          "en": "we see Schwarzmuller here at the beginning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.38,
          "end": 194.46,
          "en": "and if I enter Maximilian,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.46,
          "end": 196.96,
          "en": "we see Maximilian Schwarzmuller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.96,
          "end": 200.03,
          "en": "Now since I'm using a method we can even add an if check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.03,
          "end": 204.823,
          "en": "and check if this name is currently empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.85,
          "end": 210.23,
          "en": "and if it is empty we just return an empty string here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 210.23,
          "end": 215.23,
          "en": "so that we only add Schwarzmuller if the name is not empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.44,
          "end": 217.48,
          "en": "So here we leveraged the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.48,
          "end": 221.25,
          "en": "that we're having a method to return different values based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.25,
          "end": 223.4,
          "en": "on different values and name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 223.4,
          "end": 226.02,
          "en": "And with that if I saved as a reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 226.02,
          "end": 228.94,
          "en": "we make sure that we initially don't see anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 228.94,
          "end": 232.86,
          "en": "and we only see full name with Schwarzmuller included",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 232.86,
          "end": 235.02,
          "en": "if I did enter a real name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 235.02,
          "end": 238.373,
          "en": "and as soon as that's empty again, the full name is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.28,
          "end": 240.78,
          "en": "So that's pretty nice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 243.307,
          "en": "however, it's not the best way of doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 243.307,
          "end": 246.53,
          "en": "\"Now why is that not the best way of doing it?\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.53,
          "end": 250.09,
          "en": "Well, if I type here we update the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.09,
          "end": 252.18,
          "en": "and output down there, that's good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.18,
          "end": 256,
          "en": "The problem is if I press this counter button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256,
          "end": 257.95,
          "en": "we don't see a problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 257.95,
          "end": 260.65,
          "en": "but behind the scenes Vue does something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 260.65,
          "end": 262.94,
          "en": "which is not ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 262.94,
          "end": 265.13,
          "en": "When we change the counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 265.13,
          "end": 268.53,
          "en": "Vue basically tries to find out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 268.53,
          "end": 273.53,
          "en": "where on this page, it needs to update the rendered page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 275,
          "end": 278.36,
          "en": "So for example, if the counter changes Vue sees",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.36,
          "end": 280.92,
          "en": "that in this paragraph we're using to counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 280.92,
          "end": 285.02,
          "en": "and hence it needs to well update this part here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.02,
          "end": 288.58,
          "en": "on the real page, that's exactly why we use Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.58,
          "end": 291.87,
          "en": "it updates the page for us automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.87,
          "end": 296.01,
          "en": "The problem is if we call a method like this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 296.01,
          "end": 301.01,
          "en": "this method will also be re-executed by Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.04,
          "end": 304.32,
          "en": "whenever anything on the page changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.32,
          "end": 308.52,
          "en": "because Vue can't know what this method does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 308.52,
          "end": 310.2,
          "en": "It doesn't know wherever,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 310.2,
          "end": 313.46,
          "en": "maybe the counter gets used in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.46,
          "end": 315.23,
          "en": "Well, if the counter changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.23,
          "end": 317.77,
          "en": "and this method maybe uses the counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.77,
          "end": 321.14,
          "en": "this method should be re-executed, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 321.14,
          "end": 324.49,
          "en": "Well, and for that reason Vue goes ahead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 324.49,
          "end": 327.64,
          "en": "and re-executes any method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 327.64,
          "end": 330.57,
          "en": "you're using anywhere in your HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 331.48,
          "end": 336.13,
          "en": "between curly braces, or with the bind, or with the HTML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 336.13,
          "end": 340.74,
          "en": "so any non-event bound method will be re-executed by Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 340.74,
          "end": 343.39,
          "en": "whenever anything on the screen changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 343.39,
          "end": 347.3,
          "en": "Even if like in this case, we know that in this method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.3,
          "end": 348.69,
          "en": "we're not using the counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 348.69,
          "end": 351.06,
          "en": "We know it, but Vue doesn't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 351.06,
          "end": 354.62,
          "en": "And from a performance perspective, that's not so great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 354.62,
          "end": 356.11,
          "en": "And we can see this by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 356.11,
          "end": 360.033,
          "en": "we can add a console log here running again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 362.21,
          "end": 365.97,
          "en": "and if I now, increase this a little bit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 365.97,
          "end": 367.86,
          "en": "open up the browser developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 367.86,
          "end": 370.75,
          "en": "and go to the JavaScript console part,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 370.75,
          "end": 373.16,
          "en": "you will see that if I reload here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 373.16,
          "end": 375.8,
          "en": "we see running again initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 375.8,
          "end": 378.92,
          "en": "but if I change to counter, we also see it running again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 378.92,
          "end": 381.33,
          "en": "being executed over and over again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 381.33,
          "end": 384.08,
          "en": "even though we just changed to counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 384.08,
          "end": 386.91,
          "en": "Still outputFullname was executed again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 386.91,
          "end": 389.423,
          "en": "for the reasons I just specified.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 391.23,
          "end": 393.31,
          "en": "And that's not a back, that's how Vue works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 393.31,
          "end": 397.71,
          "en": "And that's why methods are not the best solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 397.71,
          "end": 402.24,
          "en": "for outputting some dynamically calculated value like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 402.24,
          "end": 404.113,
          "en": "but what is a better solution then?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
